+**Keeping up with upstream: what each release changed**
+
+Each new upstream release can stop the patches applying: new settings take the same slots, new menu sections take the same numbers, and files the patches touch get rewritten or removed. When that happens the kit stops without changing anything, the series is rebased onto the new release by hand, built and checked against upstream’s own checks and host tests, and a new kit is committed. [Section 9 of the project PDF](docs/nas/keeping-up-with-upstream.md) has the details (the same text as in the [project PDF](M5StackTab5QMX+SharedOverNetwork.pdf), page 13).
+
+| Release (ported) | What stopped the patches | How it was resolved |
+|---|---|---|
+| v1.20.5 (2026-10-23) | Settings bits 143-144 taken; upstream sends every CAT command through its own `cat_tx()` | Relay setting moved to bit 145; the network transport became a branch inside `cat_tx()`; an empty keyer-speed patch dropped |
+| v1.21.0 (2026-10-25) | Bits 145-146; drawer section 52; five new "Switch to …" entries in the web Radio menu | Relay setting bit 147; Radio source drawer section 53, placed under the new menu entries |
